          "case_name": "In re Shawn B.",
          "citation": "218 Ill. App. 3d 374, 578 N.E.2d 269 (1991)",
          "court": "Appellate Court of Illinois",
          "year": 1991,
          "date_decided": "1991-08-14",
          "holding": "The court affirmed as modified an order vacating DCFS guardianship and terminating wardship of an eighteen-year-old, directing that the public guardian be given leave to petition for reinstatement of wardship and guardianship at any time before the youth's twenty-first birthday.",
          "relevance": "Holds that a young person may not simply be discharged at eighteen without regard to readiness for independent living, and preserves reinstatement of wardship up to twenty-one.",
          "quote": "There was no evidence in the record to indicate that Shawn B. possessed the skills and autonomy to successfully undertake independent living.",
